.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payouts-prepare - Prepare a payout without signing it (shows the exact amount)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payouts prepare [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Ask the gateway to build a payout's unsigned transfer, and print the pending
payout: the exact amount (base units and amount_formatted) — the way to see what
"all" or a proof comes to — and unsigned_transaction, the EIP-1559 transaction to
sign. Nothing is signed or sent.

.PP
Then either 'payouts submit \&' (verify, sign with -p, submit), or sign it with
a wallet of your own and report the hash with 'payouts report-hash  \&'.
Check unsigned_transaction before signing it elsewhere: 'to' must be the token,
\&'data' transfer(destination address, amount), value 0.

.PP
A prepare replaces the destination's pending payout while it is unsigned; leave it
and it stays pending until replaced or cancelled ('payouts cancel \&'). The
session must be the destination's wallet ('rail0 auth login').


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--amount\fP=""
	Decimal in token units (e.g. 250.00), or 'all' for the balance minus the refund reserve

.PP
\fB-d\fP, \fB--destination\fP=""
	Destination id ('rail0 payouts destinations')

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for prepare

.PP
\fB--proof\fP[=false]
	Send the proof transfer (the gateway sets its amount) instead of a payout


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payouts prepare --destination <destination_id> --amount all
  rail0 payouts prepare --destination <destination_id> --proof
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payouts(1)\fP
